diff --git a/features/todos.feature b/features/todos.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..541de21
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/todos.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,313 @@
+Feature: Todo List Management
+  As a user
+  I want to manage a todo list
+  So that I can track tasks I need to complete
+
+  Rule: Application boots with an empty state
+
+  Scenario: App initialises with no todos
+    Given the app is loaded
+    Then the main section is hidden
+    And the footer is hidden
+    And the todo list is empty
+    And the todo-count reads "0 items left"
+
+  Rule: New todos are created from the header input
+
+  Scenario: Create a new todo
+    Given the app is loaded
+    When I type "Buy groceries" into the new-todo input and press Enter
+    Then the todo list contains 1 item
+    And the new item has title "Buy groceries"
+    And the new item is not completed
+    And the new-todo input is cleared
+    And the main section is visible
+    And the footer is visible
+    And the todo-count reads "1 item left"
+
+  Scenario: Create multiple todos
+    Given the app is loaded
+    When I type "Buy groceries" into the new-todo input and press Enter
+    And I type "Walk the dog" into the new-todo input and press Enter
+    And I type "Write code" into the new-todo input and press Enter
+    Then the todo list contains 3 items
+    And the todo-count reads "3 items left"
+
+  Scenario: Trimming whitespace from new todo title
+    Given the app is loaded
+    When I type "   Trim me   " into the new-todo input and press Enter
+    Then the new item has title "Trim me"
+
+  Scenario: Empty todo is not created
+    Given the app is loaded
+    When I type "   " into the new-todo input and press Enter
+    Then the todo list is empty
+
+  Rule: Todos can be marked as completed
+
+  Scenario: Toggle a todo as completed
+    Given the app is loaded with todos:
+      | title        |
+      | Buy groceries |
+      | Walk the dog  |
+    When I toggle the "Buy groceries" todo
+    Then the "Buy groceries" todo is marked completed
+    And the "Walk the dog" todo is not completed
+    And the todo-count reads "1 item left"
+
+  Scenario: Toggle a completed todo back to active
+    Given the app is loaded with todos:
+      | title        | completed |
+      | Buy groceries | true      |
+      | Walk the dog  | false     |
+    When I toggle the "Buy groceries" todo
+    Then the "Buy groceries" todo is not completed
+    And the todo-count reads "2 items left"
+
+  Rule: Mark all as complete toggles every todo
+
+  Scenario: Mark all as complete checks all todos
+    Given the app is loaded with todos:
+      | title        |
+      | Buy groceries |
+      | Walk the dog  |
+      | Write code    |
+    When I toggle the mark-all-complete checkbox
+    Then every todo is marked completed
+    And the mark-all-complete checkbox is checked
+    And the todo-count reads "0 items left"
+
+  Scenario: Mark all as complete unchecks when any todo is unchecked
+    Given the app is loaded with todos:
+      | title        | completed |
+      | Buy groceries | true      |
+      | Walk the dog  | true      |
+      | Write code    | true      |
+    When I toggle the "Walk the dog" todo
+    Then the mark-all-complete checkbox is not checked
+
+  Scenario: Clear completed button unchecks all after clearing
+    Given the app is loaded with todos:
+      | title        | completed |
+      | Buy groceries | true      |
+      | Walk the dog  | false     |
+      | Write code    | true      |
+    When I click the clear-completed button
+    Then the mark-all-complete checkbox is not checked
+
+  Rule: Each todo item has interactive controls
+
+  Scenario: A todo shows the destroy button on hover
+    Given the app is loaded with todos:
+      | title        |
+      | Buy groceries |
+    When I hover over the "Buy groceries" todo
+    Then the destroy button for "Buy groceries" is visible
+
+  Scenario: Delete a todo with the destroy button
+    Given the app is loaded with todos:
+      | title        |
+      | Buy groceries |
+      | Walk the dog  |
+    When I click the destroy button for "Buy groceries"
+    Then the todo list contains 1 item
+    And the todo list does not contain "Buy groceries"
+
+  Rule: Double-clicking a todo label activates editing mode
+
+  Scenario: Double-click a todo to edit
+    Given the app is loaded with todos:
+      | title        |
+      | Buy groceries |
+    When I double-click the label of "Buy groceries"
+    Then the "Buy groceries" todo is in editing mode
+    And the edit input is focused
+    And the edit input value is "Buy groceries"
+    And the toggle checkbox is hidden
+    And the destroy button is hidden
+
+  Scenario: Save edit on Enter
+    Given the app is loaded with todos:
+      | title        |
+      | Buy groceries |
+    When I double-click the label of "Buy groceries"
+    And I type "Buy organic groceries" into the edit input and press Enter
+    Then the "Buy groceries" todo is not in editing mode
+    And the "Buy organic groceries" todo exists
+    And the "Buy groceries" todo does not exist
+
+  Scenario: Save edit on blur
+    Given the app is loaded with todos:
+      | title        |
+      | Buy groceries |
+    When I double-click the label of "Buy groceries"
+    And I type "Buy organic groceries" into the edit input and blur
+    Then the "Buy groceries" todo is not in editing mode
+    And the "Buy organic groceries" todo exists
+
+  Scenario: Empty edit destroys the todo
+    Given the app is loaded with todos:
+      | title        |
+      | Buy groceries |
+      | Walk the dog  |
+    When I double-click the label of "Buy groceries"
+    And I type "" into the edit input and press Enter
+    Then the todo list contains 1 item
+    And the todo list does not contain "Buy groceries"
+
+  Scenario: Trimmed empty edit destroys the todo
+    Given the app is loaded with todos:
+      | title        |
+      | Buy groceries |
+    When I double-click the label of "Buy groceries"
+    And I type "   " into the edit input and press Enter
+    Then the todo list is empty
+
+  Scenario: Escape discards edit changes
+    Given the app is loaded with todos:
+      | title        |
+      | Buy groceries |
+    When I double-click the label of "Buy groceries"
+    And I type "Buy organic groceries" into the edit input and press Escape
+    Then the "Buy groceries" todo is not in editing mode
+    And the todo item title is "Buy groceries"
+
+  Rule: The todo-count shows the number of active items
+
+  Scenario: Counter pluralizes correctly
+    Given the app is loaded with todos:
+      | title        |
+      | Buy groceries |
+    When I check the todo-count
+    Then it reads "1 item left"
+    When I create a todo "Walk the dog"
+    Then it reads "2 items left"
+    When I toggle the "Buy groceries" todo
+    Then it reads "1 item left"
+    When I toggle the "Walk the dog" todo
+    Then it reads "0 items left"
+
+  Scenario: Counter wraps count in a strong tag
+    Given the app is loaded with todos:
+      | title        |
+      | Buy groceries |
+      | Walk the dog  |
+    When I check the todo-count element
+    Then the count number is wrapped in a <strong> tag
+
+  Rule: Clear completed removes completed todos
+
+  Scenario: Clear completed removes all completed items
+    Given the app is loaded with todos:
+      | title        | completed |
+      | Buy groceries | true      |
+      | Walk the dog  | false     |
+      | Write code    | true      |
+    When I click the clear-completed button
+    Then the todo list contains 1 item
+    And the todo list does not contain "Buy groceries"
+    And the todo list does not contain "Write code"
+    And the todo list contains "Walk the dog"
+
+  Scenario: Clear completed button is hidden when no completed todos
+    Given the app is loaded with todos:
+      | title        |
+      | Buy groceries |
+      | Walk the dog  |
+    Then the clear-completed button is hidden
+
+  Scenario: Clear completed button is visible when there are completed todos
+    Given the app is loaded with todos:
+      | title        | completed |
+      | Buy groceries | true      |
+      | Walk the dog  | false     |
+    Then the clear-completed button is visible
+
+  Rule: Todos persist across page reloads via localStorage
+
+  Scenario: Todos are persisted to localStorage
+    Given the app is loaded with todos:
+      | title        |
+      | Buy groceries |
+      | Walk the dog  |
+    When I reload the app
+    Then the todo list contains 2 items
+    And the "Buy groceries" todo exists
+    And the "Walk the dog" todo exists
+
+  Scenario: Completed state is persisted to localStorage
+    Given the app is loaded with todos:
+      | title        |
+      | Buy groceries |
+      | Walk the dog  |
+    When I toggle the "Buy groceries" todo
+    And I reload the app
+    Then the "Buy groceries" todo is marked completed
+    And the "Walk the dog" todo is not completed
+
+  Scenario: localStorage key is "todos-javascript"
+    Given the app is loaded
+    When I type "Test" into the new-todo input and press Enter
+    Then the localStorage key "todos-javascript" contains the todo data
+    And each stored item has keys "id", "title", and "completed"
+
+  Scenario: Editing state is not persisted
+    Given the app is loaded with todos:
+      | title        |
+      | Buy groceries |
+    When I double-click the label of "Buy groceries"
+    And I reload the app
+    Then no todo is in editing mode
+
+  Rule: Routing filters the displayed todos
+
+  Scenario: Default route shows all todos
+    Given the app is loaded with todos:
+      | title        | completed |
+      | Buy groceries | false     |
+      | Walk the dog  | true      |
+    Then the "#/" route is active
+    And the All filter link has the "selected" class
+    And the todo list contains 2 items
+
+  Scenario: Active route shows only active todos
+    Given the app is loaded with todos:
+      | title        | completed |
+      | Buy groceries | false     |
+      | Walk the dog  | true      |
+    When I navigate to "#/active"
+    Then the Active filter link has the "selected" class
+    And the todo list contains 1 item
+    And the visible items include "Buy groceries"
+    And the visible items do not include "Walk the dog"
+
+  Scenario: Completed route shows only completed todos
+    Given the app is loaded with todos:
+      | title        | completed |
+      | Buy groceries | false     |
+      | Walk the dog  | true      |
+      | Write code    | true      |
+    When I navigate to "#/completed"
+    Then the Completed filter link has the "selected" class
+    And the todo list contains 2 items
+    And the visible items include "Walk the dog"
+    And the visible items include "Write code"
+    And the visible items do not include "Buy groceries"
+
+  Scenario: Todos update when completed while filtered
+    Given the app is loaded with todos:
+      | title        | completed |
+      | Buy groceries | false     |
+      | Walk the dog  | true      |
+    When I navigate to "#/active"
+    And I toggle the "Buy groceries" todo
+    Then the visible items do not include "Buy groceries"
+
+  Scenario: Active filter is persisted across reloads
+    Given the app is loaded with todos:
+      | title        |
+      | Buy groceries |
+      | Walk the dog  |
+    When I navigate to "#/active"
+    And I reload the app
+    Then the Active filter link has the "selected" class
\ No newline at end of file
